    <meta name="description" content="A practical guide to Indian e-Visas and Sikkim permits for Feels Like Om guests travelling to West Sikkim." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/type-system.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/">Feels Like Om</a>
      <nav class="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary class="active">ABOUT</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/about/our-story">Our story</a>
            <a href="/about/getting-to-sikkim">Getting to Sikkim</a>
            <a href="/about/visa-and-permits" aria-current="page">Visa and permits</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary>JOURNEYS</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/journeys/the-flagship">The Flagship</a>
            <a href="/journeys/how-to-embrace-suffering">To Be Free</a>
            <a href="/journeys#feels-like-home">Feels Like Home</a>
            <a href="/journeys#way-of-the-yaks">Way of the Yaks</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a href="/reflections">REFLECTIONS</a>
        <a href="/contact">CONTACT</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="page-hero">
        <div class="wide">
          <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p>
          <h1>Visa and permits</h1>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="permit-section">
        <div class="wide permit-grid">
          <div class="permit-image image-placeholder portrait"><span>Sample Indian e-Visa</span></div>
          <div class="permit-copy">
            <h2>Indian e-Visa</h2>
            <p>All guests should check if they require a visa to enter India.</p>
            <p>For Singaporeans, a visa is required.</p>
            <p>You can apply online via India’s <a href="https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/evisa/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">official e-visa portal</a>. The application itself usually takes around 15 minutes to complete.</p>
            <p>The approval process typically takes 24 to 72 hours, but we strongly recommend applying at least a month in advance in case of delays.</p>
            <p>The cost of the tourist visa varies. Please refer to the official website for the most updated information.</p>
            <p>We can guide you through the visa application process.</p>
            <p>You will need to prepare:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>A PDF copy of your passport biodata page, with at least six months’ validity</li>
              <li>A JPG of your passport-size photo</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="permit-section alt">
        <div class="wide permit-grid reverse">
          <div class="permit-copy">
            <h2>Sikkim Permit</h2>
            <p>In addition to your Indian visa, foreign nationals are required to obtain an Inner Line Permit (ILP) to enter Sikkim.</p>
            <p>The ILP is free of charge and can be easily applied for. Your driver will stop at the checkpost for you to apply for the ILP.</p>
            <p>You will need to prepare:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Original passport</li>
              <li>One passport-size photo</li>
              <li>A photocopy of your passport biodata page</li>
              <li>A photocopy of your granted e-visa</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The process is usually very quick and fuss-free. Make sure you keep all the required documents ready in your carry-on bag.</p>
            <aside class="important">
              <h3>Important</h3>
              <p>Travellers of certain nationalities, and in some cases people born in certain places, may require prior approval from India’s Ministry of Home Affairs before a Sikkim permit can be issued. Requirements can change, so check the latest official guidance before travelling.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>
          <div class="permit-image image-placeholder portrait"><span>Sample Sikkim Inner Line Permit</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
